  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 PM MDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nExtreme heat continues through today with many locations in\nlower elevations around 100 or slightly above. Will have some\nbreezy conditions as well with 10 to 20 mph winds this evening\nin the Snake River Plain and higher elevations as well. Will\nfinally start to see a cool down Sunday and into next week as a\ndry upper level trof moves through Idaho and flow aloft turns\nfrom southwest to northwest allowing some Canadian air to filter\ninto Idaho. Highs tomorrow mainly in the low to mid 90s lower\nelevations with very breezy conditions once again with speeds\nsustained again 10 to 20 mph with gusts around 30 mph in many\nlocations. By Monday low elevations highs in the 80s and below\nnormal for once and mountains mainly in the 70s. Cooldown will\nbe short lived with upper ridge rebuilding Wednesday into next\nweekend with high temperatures well into the 90s in lower\nelevations by Thursday. It does appear to be a very dry 8 days\nwith no precipitation in the forecast grids through next\nSaturday.",
